 growth in the northern high latitudes from 1981 to 1991. Nature 386, 698\u2013702 (1997).","journal-title":"Nature"},{"key":"1270_CR10","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"10823","DOI":"10.1073\/pnas.0501647102","volume":"102","author":"A Angert","year":"2005","unstructured":"Angert, A. et al. Drier summers cancel out the CO2 uptake enhancement induced by warmer springs. Proc. Natl Acad. Sci. USA 102, 10823\u201310827 (2005).","journal-title":"Proc. Natl Acad. Sci. USA"},{"key":"1270_CR11","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"24027","DOI":"10.1088\/1748-9326\/8\/2\/024027","volume":"8","author":"W Buermann","year":"2013","unstructured":"Buermann, W., Bikash, P. R., Jung, M., Burn, D. H. & Reichstein, M. Earlier springs decrease peak summer productivity in North American boreal forests. Environ. Res. Lett. 8, 24027 (2013).","journal-title":"Environ. Res. Lett."},{"key":"1270_CR12","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"110","DOI":"10.1038\/s41586-018-0555-7","volume":"562","author":"W Buermann","year":"2018","unstructured":"Buermann, W. et al. Widespread seasonal compensation effects of spring warming on northern plant productivity. Nature 562, 110\u2013114 (2018).","journal-title":"Nature"},{"key":"1270_CR13","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"397","DOI":"10.1038\/s41559-022-01668-4","volume":"6","author":"S Gao","year":"2022","unstructured":"Gao, S. et al. An earlier start of the thermal growing season enhances tree growth in cold humid areas but not in dry areas. Nat. Ecol. Evol. 6, 397\u2013404 (2022).","journal-title":"Nat. Ecol. Evol."},{"key":"1270_CR14","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"2117","DOI":"10.1111\/gcb.14001","volume":"24","author":"A Gonsamo","year":"2018","unstructured":"Gonsamo, A., Chen, J. M. & Ooi, Y. W. Peak season plant activity shift towards spring is reflected by increasing carbon uptake by extratropical ecosystems. Glob. Change Biol. 24, 2117\u20132128 (2018).","journal-title":"Glob. Change Biol."},